winex11: make the Win32 window follow a restore done by the window manager.

Restoring a minimized Cubase window from the taskbar took many clicks.
The window manager's WM_STATE change to NormalState arrives with no request
pending; the driver posts WM_WINE_WINDOW_STATE_CHANGED and only the message
handler brings the Win32 style back from WS_MINIMIZE. Until then every
SetWindowPos of the app runs X11DRV_WindowPosChanged, which derives the
desired WM state from the still minimized style and iconifies the window
again. Remember that the window manager restored the window and, until the
style has lost WS_MINIMIZE, turn the IconicState derived from the style into
NormalState (the result of get_desired_wm_state, not a style with the bit
removed: the minimized rectangle is unmapped and that gave WithdrawnState).

The restore itself had two holes. A maximized window returned SC_MAXIMIZE
without activating, and a disabled window (a modal dialog opened while it was
minimized) returned nothing at all, because WM_SYSCOMMAND is ignored by
disabled windows, so it stayed WS_MINIMIZE while X showed it. Activate in the
maximized case, and restore a disabled window directly with ShowWindow.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/x11drv.h
@@ -712,6 +712,7 @@
     unsigned long configure_serial;    /* serial of last pending configure request */
     unsigned long net_wm_icon_serial;  /* serial of last pending _NET_WM_ICON request */
     unsigned long state_locks;         /* X11 state requests lock while updating win32 state */
+    BOOL wm_restored;                  /* the window manager restored a minimized window, win32 still has to follow */
 };
 
 extern struct x11drv_win_data *get_win_data( HWND hwnd );
